## 4. Input vs. Output Token Cost Breakdown

### Classifier
- Input: system prompt (~850 tokens) + user message (~50–200 tokens) = ~900–1050 tokens
- Output: JSON ~80–150 tokens (capped at 900)
- Input/output ratio: 6:1 to 13:1

### Knowledge Planner
- Input: system prompt (~280 tokens) + JSON payload with user_message + classification + selected_knowledge_agents + knowledge_excerpts (up to agentLimit × topK = 2 × 4 = 8 matches × 1800 chars each ≈ 3600–4000 tokens of excerpts alone)
- Total input estimate: ~4500–5000 tokens
- Output: JSON plan, capped at 2200 tokens
- This is running on gpt-4o which is 10× more expensive per token than gpt-4o-mini

### Reranker
- Input: system prompt (~180 tokens) + JSON of candidates
  - Each candidate: 1800 chars ≈ ~450 tokens
  - Default: up to 40 candidates before topK filter = ~18 000 input tokens just for candidate text
  - Plus query, topK, scores, metadata overhead: add ~1000 tokens
  - Estimated total input: **~19 000 tokens per rerank call**
- Output: ranked JSON array, capped at 4096 (actual output is small ~500–800 tokens)
- Input/output ratio: 24:1 — **input dominates cost**

### Main Agent
- Input: system prompt (~1500 tokens) + memory (~200–500 tokens) + mainPayload JSON which includes:
  - retrieval_context: up to 12 records × 1800 chars ≈ ~4800 tokens (up to 50 records on list/investigation = ~20 000 tokens)
  - retrieval_results: same records duplicated in full JSON form (higher than retrieval_context)
  - graph_context: up to 12 relationships
  - project_graph_findings: summarized version
  - knowledge_plan: full plan JSON
  - tool_results: all tool calls (can include alert, meetings, emails, submittals results)
- Estimated total input on a typical RAG turn: **~12 000–30 000 tokens**
- Output: full Hebrew answer, capped at 4096 tokens
- Running on gpt-4o — **this is the single largest cost item**

### Alert Agent
- Input: system prompt (~120 tokens) + user content = date + query + 20 results JSON (each result can be large)
- Estimated total input: ~3000–8000 tokens
- Output: formatted list, capped at 2200 tokens
- Model defaults to gpt-4o (via models.main fallback) — unnecessary for a retrieval summary task

### QA Agent
- Input: system prompt (~500 tokens) + entire workflow_log JSON (can be 10 000–50 000 tokens depending on run)
- Output: JSON report, capped at 3000 tokens
- Running on gpt-4o by default

### QA Trend
- Input: all QA reports concatenated (grows over time)
- Hardcoded: temperature 0.1, maxTokens 3000 — **ignores config.ai.qa settings**
- Running on gpt-4o

