## 6. Avoidable Call Analysis

| Agent | Can It Be Avoided? | Condition |
|---|---|---|
| Classifier | No — required for routing | Could be replaced by heuristics for clearly simple messages |
| Knowledge Planner | **Yes** | The `professional` flag is set by classifier. If classifier already determined professional=false, planner never runs. Additional savings: if KB search returns zero matches, LLM call is already skipped (fallback returns early). |
| Reranker | **Partially** | If hybrid search returns fewer candidates than topK, reranker still sends all of them. Reducing `retrieval.candidates` from 40 to 20 would halve reranker input cost. |
| Alert Agent LLM call | **Yes** | If results count is 0, the LLM call still runs and just produces "no alerts found." A short-circuit check (`if (!results.length) return noAlertsAnswer`) would save the call. |
| Main Agent | No — core of the system | Reducing retrieval_context records and not duplicating retrieval_results in the payload would reduce input tokens significantly. |
| QA Trend | Only on demand | No change needed |
| Timeline Link Agent | Only on smart=true | No change needed |

