## STEP 7 — Pass / Fail Decision Criteria

After completing all profile runs, make these decisions:

**Profile A passes if ALL of the following are true:**
- Q1 routes to Lite Agent in all runs
- Q2 answer is factual with source links
- Q3 Knowledge Planner ran and produced valid JSON
- Q4 returns a ranked list (not a single name)
- Q5 sources are correct or missing is clearly stated
- Q6 QA report is complete and specific
- No answers are truncated mid-sentence
- No "no information found" false negatives

**Profile B passes if:**
- All Profile A pass criteria hold
- Q3 Knowledge Planner JSON on gpt-4o-mini is complete (not garbled or missing keys)
- Q4 ranked list is as complete as baseline (same supplier count or close)
- Q5 factual accuracy is comparable to baseline
- Q2 answer quality is acceptable compared to baseline (not notably vaguer)

**Profile B partially fails if:**
- Q3 planner JSON is missing keys or truncated → consider raising ai.knowledgePlanner.maxTokens or keeping gpt-4o for planner only
- Q4 returns fewer items than baseline → consider raising rerankTopK or keeping gpt-4o for main only
- Specific questions get worse while others hold → targeted fix, not full rollback

**Profile C is expected to fail** on Q3, Q4, Q5 — document which failures appear and at what threshold.

